of \\(\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\\):\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\implies \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\cos \\gamma = -\\left( \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\right) = -\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\left(1 - \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right) = -\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\left(\\frac{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{\\cos \\gamma} = \\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{-\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\left(\\frac{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)} = \\frac{1}{-\\left(\\frac{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)} = -\\frac{3}{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]\n\nTo rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{3}{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}} \\cdot \\frac{3 + 2\\sqrt{3}}{3 + 2\\sqrt{3}} = -\\frac{3(3 + 2\\sqrt{3})}{(3 - 2\\sqrt{3})(3 + 2\\sqrt{3})} = -\\frac{3(3 + 2\\sqrt{3})}{9 - 12} = -\\frac{3(3 + 2\\sqrt{3})}{-3} = 3 + 2\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3 + 2\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{3 + 2\\sqrt{3}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve the problem, we start by using the given information and trigonometric identities. We know that \\(\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\pi\\), which implies \\(\\gamma = \\pi - (\\alpha + \\beta)\\). Therefore, we can use the identity for the tangent of a sum of angles to express \\(\\tan \\gamma\\):\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\gamma = \\tan (\\pi - (\\alpha + \\beta)) = -\\tan (\\alpha + \\beta) = -\\frac{\\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta}{1 - \\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta}\n\\]\n\nWe are also given that \\(\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = \\csc \\frac{\\pi}{3} = \\csc 60^\\circ = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\). Let \\(x = \\tan \\alpha\\) and \\(y = \\tan \\beta\\). Then \\(xy = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\). Using the tangent addition formula, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\gamma = -\\frac{x + y}{1 - xy} = -\\frac{x + y}{1 - \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}} = -\\frac{x + y}{\\frac{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}}{3}} = -\\frac{3(x + y)}{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]\n\nTo simplify \\(\\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{\\cos \\gamma}\\), we use the identity \\(\\cos \\gamma = -\\cos (\\alpha + \\beta) = -(\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta)\\). However, a more straightforward approach is to use the product-to-sum identities and the given information.\n\nWe know that:\n\n\\[\n\\cos \\gamma = -\\cos (\\alpha + \\beta) = -(\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta)\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\), we can express \\(\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta\\) in terms of \\(\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\\):\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\implies \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\cos \\gamma = -\\left( \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\right) = -\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\left(1 - \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right) = -\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\left(\\frac{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{\\cos \\gamma} = \\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{-\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta \\left(\\frac{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)} = \\frac{1}{-\\left(\\frac{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)} = -\\frac{3}{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]\n\nTo rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{3}{3 - 2\\sqrt{3}} \\cdot \\frac{3 + 2\\sqrt{3}}{3 + 2\\sqrt{3}} = -\\frac{3(3 + 2\\sqrt{3})}{(3 - 2\\sqrt{3})(3 + 2\\sqrt{3})} = -\\frac{3(3 + 2\\sqrt{3})}{9 - 12} = -\\frac{3(3 + 2\\sqrt{3})}{-3} = 3 + 2\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3 + 2\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]","id":"precalculus:399"}
